Tired of picking from the same handful of swatches? [b]Colors+[/b] lets you choose [b]any color you like[/b] for your characters and your blasters.
Look for the new [b]CUSTOM COLOR[/b] button under the color choices. It opens a color picker where you can drag to any shade or type in a color code, and you see the result on your character or weapon as you go.
Everything happens inside the game's own customization screens, and your colors are saved by the game itself. There's no external editor and no save-file editing.

[heading]Features[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Any color, live[/b]: a color box, a rainbow bar and a color-code box, with a live preview on your character or weapon.[/*]
[*][b]Character creator and barracks[/b]: clothing and armor, hair, skin (including species skin tones, such as Zabrak), makeup, tattoos, horns and scars.[/*]
[*][b]Droids[/b]: head, body and legs colors on astromech droids in the creator and the barracks, including BR-1.[/*]
[*][b]Armory blaster paint[/b]: give your blasters a custom Paint Color, and try it on every Location and Paint Finish before you commit.[/*]
[*][b]Apply or Cancel[/b]: nothing changes until you apply, and Cancel puts your old color back.[/*]
[*][b]Saved like any other color[/b]: your colors stay put after loading a save, and even if you remove the mod.[/*]
[*][b]Works with unlocker mods[/b]: armor wearing a color the palette no longer offers can still be changed.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Using Colors+[/heading]
Click [b]CUSTOM COLOR[/b] under a color choice. Drag in the color box and along the rainbow bar, or type a color code. [b]APPLY COLOR[/b] keeps your new color; [b]CANCEL[/b] puts the old one back.
[list]
[*][b]Main-menu creator[/b]: save your character as usual to keep your colors. If you leave without saving, your old colors come back.[/*]
[*][b]Barracks[/b]: your colors are kept as soon as you apply them, and saved with your game.[/*]
[*][b]Armory → Customize Weapon[/b]: while the picker is open you're only previewing, so try different Locations and Paint Finishes to see how your color looks on each. [b]APPLY COLOR[/b] paints the weapon for real.[/*]
[/list]
Want one of the game's own colors back? Just click its swatch.

Swapping a piece (another jacket, or a different dome on a droid) puts that piece's colors back to its own, so choose your pieces first, then your colors.

[heading]Requirements[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Star Wars Zero Company[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/9]UE4SS for Star Wars Zero Company[/url][/*]
[/list]
Colors+ has been tested on the Steam release, game builds [b]24874058[/b] and [b]25134257[/b]. Other builds may work but should be treated as unverified. EA App compatibility has not been tested.

[heading]Installation[/heading]
[b]Mod manager[/b]
Colors+ includes metadata for the community mod managers:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/29]ZCOM Mod Manager[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/121]Zero Company Mod Command[/url][/*]
[/list]
Install the downloaded ZIP through either one and make sure Colors+ is enabled.

[b]Manual installation[/b]
Make sure UE4SS is installed and working, close the game, then extract the [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder into:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/code]
The finished installation should contain:
[code]ue4ss/Mods/ColorsPlus/Scripts/main.lua[/code]
The package includes [b]enabled.txt[/b]. If your UE4SS setup doesn't pick it up, add this line to [b]ue4ss/Mods/mods.txt[/b]:
[code]ColorsPlus : 1[/code]
[b]Updating:[/b] close the game first, then install the new ZIP the same way (by hand, copy the new [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder over the old one). Only one copy of Colors+ can be installed at a time.

[b]Uninstalling[/b]
Switch Colors+ off or remove it in your mod manager, or delete the [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder. Your custom colors stay on your characters and weapons, and your saves load fine without the mod.

[heading]Compatibility[/heading]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/291]MinervaMagicka's Character Overhaul Suite[/url]: compatible.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/34]Smexy's ZCUnlocked[/url]: mostly compatible. Custom colors don't work for its Blaster Bolt or Lightsaber colors.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/134]Coppershore's Ship Paint and Hangar Lift[/url]: not tested yet.[/*]
[/list]
Colors+ should coexist with most unrelated UE4SS mods. Mods that replace the character creator, barracks or armory customization screens may conflict with its button or picker.

[heading]Known Issues[/heading]
[list]
[*]Mouse only: the buttons can't be reached with a controller.[/*]
[*]Eye colors aren't supported (eye-color options added by another mod may be).[/*]
[*]Restart the game after installing or updating Colors+. Don't use UE4SS's "Reload All Mods"; it can crash or freeze the game.[/*]
[*]Sweeping the mouse quickly across the color swatches can close the picker. Your previous color is kept; just open it again.[/*]
[*]The picker's buttons are in English only for now.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Troubleshooting[/heading]
Colors+ writes diagnostic information to two logs in its [b]ColorsPlus[/b] folder: [b]colors_plus_probe.log[/b] and [b]colors_plus_performance.log[/b]. [b]UE4SS.log[/b] remains the primary startup and crash log.
When reporting a problem, please include:
[list]
[*]Your game build[/*]
[*]Your UE4SS version[/*]
[*]Your other installed mods[/*]
[*]What you were customizing (which character or weapon) and what happened[/*]
[*][code]UE4SS.log[/code][/*]
[*][code]colors_plus_probe.log[/code] and [code]colors_plus_performance.log[/code][/*]
[/list]
The logs only contain technical details about what the mod did: no screenshots, saves or personal files. They may mention folder paths on your PC, so feel free to look them over before sending.

[heading]Source Code and Issue Reports[/heading]
Source, technical documentation and issue tracking are available on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/ColorsPlus]GitHub[/url]. You can also post in the Bugs tab here on Nexus.

